## std::fmt — Display + Debug formal mixins, plus the placeholder
## Formatter / FmtError types.
##
## Wave 2 (#06.8) — migrated from resolve/stdlib/mod.rs Rust
## registrations into self-hosted library/std/src/fmt.rx.
##
## Display is the canonical interpolation mixin (`"#{x}"` lowers
## through Display::fmt). Its `fmt` carries only the method NAME (the
## Rust registration carried `["fmt"]`); the full `fmt(&self, &mut
## Formatter) -> Result[nil, FmtError]` signature lands when mixin
## default-method lowering does. Debug is the `derive Debug` target: it
## declares `to_debug -> String`, the method a derived Debug defines,
## and the compiler reads that name from this declaration.
##
## Formatter and FmtError are placeholder classes (no fields, no
## methods registered through DefKind::Method yet). The runtime
## `ruxen_fmt_*` helpers in library/runtime/fmt.c back the
## constructor + dispatch wired by Phase D's lower_interpolation.
## v1 deliberately keeps the public surface empty — see
## docs/specs/stdlib/fmt.spec.md.
mixin Display
  def fmt
end

## A derived `Debug` defines `to_debug -> String`, which interpolation calls
## for a Debug value; the compiler reads the method name from this declaration.
mixin Debug
  def to_debug -> String
end

## std::fmt::Formatter — buffered accumulator that `Display::fmt` /
## `Debug::fmt` write into. Phase E-rest 3 of #06.95 migrated the
## constructor + low-level write surface from `runtime_table` arms
## into class-body lib decls. `new_with_spec` and `precision` stay
## on runtime_table because their `Option[USize]` typeck contract
## doesn't yet round-trip through the FFI alias path (the C runtime
## uses an `int64_t -1` sentinel for nil, which the lib decl
## syntax can't yet express).
##
## FmtError is declared BEFORE Formatter so Formatter.write_str /
## write_char's `-> Result[nil, FmtError]` return type resolves at
## parse time.
class FmtError

end

class Formatter
  lib "runtime/fmt.c"
    def self.new as "ruxen_fmt_formatter_new" -> Formatter
    def free as "ruxen_fmt_formatter_free" -> nil
    def write_str as "ruxen_fmt_formatter_write_str"(s: &String) -> Result[nil, FmtError]
    def write_char as "ruxen_fmt_formatter_write_char"(ch: Int) -> Result[nil, FmtError]
    def buffer as "ruxen_fmt_formatter_buffer" -> String
    def size as "ruxen_fmt_formatter_len" -> Int
  end
end
